From: NAOS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] rsa: match Rockchip maximum-length PSS signing salt

Match the signing convention used by the existing RK3588 secure boot flow.
OpenSSL's -2 signing value selects the largest PSS salt permitted by the key.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Rockchip boot-chain signing compatibility]
---
diff --git a/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c b/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
--- a/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
+++ b/lib/rsa/rsa-sign.c
@@ -455,11 +455,9 @@ static int rsa_sign_with_key(EVP_PKEY *pkey, struct padding_algo *padding_algo,
 			goto err_sign;
 		}
 
-		/* Per RFC 3447 (and convention) the Typical salt length is the
-		 * length of the output of the digest algorithm.
-		 */
+		/* Rockchip tools sign with the maximum key-permitted salt. */
 		if (EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_rsa_pss_saltlen(ckey,
-						     checksum_algo->checksum_len) <= 0) {
+						     -2) <= 0) {
 			ret = rsa_err("Signer salt length setup failed");
 			goto err_sign;
 		}
